WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.719
Consider the roadside ditch provided. Using the chart excerpt from the

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:12.480
Ashto roadside design guide, determine the steepest allowable force lobe in

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.359
units of vertical slash horizontal. So in this problem all we need to do is use

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:22.480
the Ashto chart provided to correctly identify the steepest allowable

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.879
force lobe in units of vertical slash horizontal. First we need to recognize

00:00:28.879 --> 00:00:32.700
that force lobe is the first slope leading down from the roadway to the

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.119
bottom of the v-ditch and the back slope is the second slope leading back up to

00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:44.659
the ground surface. So we can draw a line from the back slope given which is 1

00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:51.799
colon 5 or 1 vertical unit to 5 horizontal units. Once we reach the edge of the

00:00:51.799 --> 00:00:57.219
preferred channel cross section we can draw the line either up or down. The

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:02.700
problem asks for units of vertical slash horizontal. So let's draw this

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:10.980
line downward. As can be seen we land somewhere between 0.3 and 0.2.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.460
Typically it makes sense to round to the more conservative slope. So let's pick

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.819
the smaller of the two numbers given. This would be less than the max allowable

00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:26.539
foreslope according to the chart but rounding the other way would exceed our

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.180
limitations instead. You will notice that technically 1 colon 5 is the same

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:40.580
slope as 0.2. But the problem asks for units of v slash h so we will pick 0.2

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.780
instead. And that's all it takes to solve this problem.
